<template>
    <heading>Select/Create Project Dialog</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>dialog</li>
        <li>project selection</li>
        <li>project creation</li>
        <li>modal</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>
            This article defines the Select/Create Project dialog. Its bundle
            name matches the dialog template's <code>id</code>, so the parent
            dialog-template container can insert it with a code reference.
            The action names are handled by the generic modal dialog operation.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>LP5-Dialog-SelectCreateProject</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
<template id="LP5-Dialog-SelectCreateProject">
    <style>
        .LP5-SelectCreateProject {
            max-width: 25rem;
            padding: 1.25rem;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .LP5-SelectCreateProject h2 {
            margin: 0 0 1rem;
            font-size: 1.25rem;
        }

        .LP5-SelectCreateProject .dialog-buttons {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 1rem;
        }

        .LP5-SelectCreateProject button {
            padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem;
            font-size: 1rem;
        }

        .LP5-SelectCreateProject [role="alert"] {
            color: #a00;
        }
    </style>
    <dialog class="LP5-SelectCreateProject"
            aria-labelledby="LP5-SelectCreateProject-title">
        <h2 id="LP5-SelectCreateProject-title">Select or Create a Project</h2>
        <div class="dialog-buttons">
            <button type="button" autofocus data-action="Select">Select</button>
            <button type="button" data-action="Create">Create</button>
        </div>
        <p data-name="selectionError" role="alert"></p>
    </dialog>
</template>
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
